From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:33:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: Build servoshell on QuickJS, and run WPT with it nightly

The QuickJS workflow patches mozjs to openharmony-rs/servo-quickjs (a
pinned commit, or a branch, tag or full commit hash given to a manual
run), builds a release servoshell with js-quickjs, runs the smoketest
and runs WPT through linux-wpt.yml. WPT compares against the
SpiderMonkey expectations, so its unexpected results are the gaps of the
QuickJS backend: the WPT jobs pass regardless, and the
stable-unexpected-results-linux artifact lists the gaps. It runs nightly
and by hand. linux-common.yml can't be reused because it builds with
--locked, and the patch changes Cargo.lock.

Pull requests and the merge queue build it too, in addition to the
SpiderMonkey build: the try configuration gets a quickjs job
(try_parser.py, dispatch-workflow.yml), which runs the workflow in the
job's profile (checked-release) without WPT. pr_jobs.py adds it where
the OHOS build and the whole WPT suite run, and for changes to the
workflow itself; the merge queue runs it with linux-wpt and ohos. The
job gets no secrets, so QuickJS results never reach the intermittent
tracker. The servo-quickjs commit is pinned (SERVO_QUICKJS_REF), so that
updates there don't change what older commits build with; it is bumped
with mozjs at syncs. A try run with both linux-wpt and a QuickJS WPT run
would upload two artifacts of the same name.

Validation: The patch step run locally against a file:// clone of servo-quickjs (`mozjs-0.26`, 7b4141b): it resolves the branch to the commit, Cargo.lock then takes mozjs 0.26.7 and servo-quickjs from it, `./mach build --profile release --features js-quickjs` builds and `xvfb-run ./mach smoketest --profile release` passes. The ref resolution was checked against a scratch repository with branches main and wip/main, an annotated and a lightweight tag: only exact branches and tags and full hashes resolve. For the pull request job: the try_parser and pr_jobs tests pass, with a new case for changes to the workflow alone; actionlint with shellcheck reports nothing new for quickjs.yml, dispatch-workflow.yml and main.yml; the merge queue string yields the jobs Linux (WPT), OpenHarmony and Linux QuickJS. On 7f6279eb9b9 with the pinned servo-quickjs commit (72fa2b6697a; its tree was built), the QuickJS build and smoketest pass with --profile checked-release, the pull request job's, and release, the nightly's. The patch step resolves the pin to itself and still takes branches and tags from a manual run, and cargo resolves the pinned rev to mozjs 0.26.7. The workflow itself has not run yet: the pinned commit is not public until servo-quickjs main is pushed.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written by the agent, and its build steps tested locally by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 .github/workflows/dispatch-workflow.yml |  10 ++
 .github/workflows/main.yml              |   2 +-
 .github/workflows/quickjs.yml           | 133 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 python/servo/pr_jobs.py                 |  28 ++++-
 python/servo/try_parser.py              |   7 +-
 5 files changed, 173 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 .github/workflows/quickjs.yml

diff --git a/.github/workflows/dispatch-workflow.yml b/.github/workflows/dispatch-workflow.yml
index 96cb0ffe805..04c0ebe0c70 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/dispatch-workflow.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/dispatch-workflow.yml
@@ -146,3 +146,13 @@ jobs:
     with:
       profile: ${{ inputs.profile }}
       bencher: ${{ inputs.bencher }}
+
+  quickjs:
+    if: ${{ inputs.workflow == 'quickjs' }}
